{"type":"text","timestamp":1794652200039,"sessionID":"ses_e2664f1aeffe9y62wg3QJH9bd4","part":{"id":"prt_1d99b4807001lSM4ZL6bzv6Lu0","messageID":"msg_1d99b1cf80011WPSKA7ihL4aYg","sessionID":"ses_e2664f1aeffe9y62wg3QJH9bd4","type":"text","text":"Let me analyze the code and understand the task better. I need to:\n1. Add `entries_b64` to the allowed orphan body fields\n2. Implement `_orphan_entries_problem` function\n3. Wire it into `cmd_monitor` where orphans are checked\n","time":{"start":1794652194823,"end":1794652200038}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794652200060,"sessionID":"ses_e2664f1aeffe9y62wg3QJH9bd4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"call-f3cc066f-ed36-4864-ab73-0db17056181b","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/record/record.py","oldString":"else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n        allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n        if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n        try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n            base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")","newString":"else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n        allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n        if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n        try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n            base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n        except ValueError:\n            raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n        if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n            if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n            for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n                if not isinstance(x, str):\n                    raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n                try:\n                    base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n                except ValueError:\n                    raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -148,15 +148,25 @@\n     if body.get(\"outcome\") not in OUTCOMES:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: outcome must be one of {OUTCOMES}\")\n     _check_digests(_need(body, \"evidence\", list, where), f\"{where}.evidence\")\n else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n-    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n+    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n     if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n     try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n         base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n     except ValueError:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n+    if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n+        if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n+            raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n+        for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n+            if not isinstance(x, str):\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n+            try:\n+                base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n+            except ValueError:\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")\n extra = set(body) - allowed\n if extra:\n     raise Bad(f\"{where}: unknown body fields {sorted(extra)}\")\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/workspace/record/record.py","patch":"Index: /workspace/record/record.py\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/record/record.py\n+++ /workspace/record/record.py\n@@ -148,15 +148,25 @@\n     if body.get(\"outcome\") not in OUTCOMES:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: outcome must be one of {OUTCOMES}\")\n     _check_digests(_need(body, \"evidence\", list, where), f\"{where}.evidence\")\n else:  # orphan: explains a Rekor attestation by the writer that the ledger doesn't hold\n-    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}\n+    allowed = {\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\", \"entries_b64\"}\n     if _need(body, \"log_index\", int, where) < 0 or not _need(body, \"reason\", str, where).strip():\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: orphan needs log_index >= 0 and a reason\")\n     try:  # the orphaned attestation's exact signed statement; monitor checks it against Rekor's payload hash\n         base64.b64decode(_need(body, \"statement_b64\", str, where), validate=True)\n     except ValueError:\n         raise Bad(f\"{where}: statement_b64 must be base64\")\n+    if \"entries_b64\" in body:\n+        if not isinstance(body[\"entries_b64\"], list):\n+            raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64 must be a list\")\n+        for i, x in enumerate(body[\"entries_b64\"]):\n+            if not isinstance(x, str):\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be a string\")\n+            try:\n+                base64.b64decode(x, validate=True)\n+            except ValueError:\n+                raise Bad(f\"{where}: entries_b64[{i}] must be base64\")\n extra = set(body) - allowed\n if extra:\n     raise Bad(f\"{where}: unknown body fields {sorted(extra)}\")\n \n","additions":11,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"workspace/record/record.py","time":{"start":1794652200036,"end":1794652200049}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me understand the task:\n\n1. I need to add a function `_orphan_entries_problem(orphan: dict, pred: dict) -> str | None` to `record/record.py`\n2. The function checks if an orphan's hidden entries match the attested range in the predicate\n3. The orphan has `body[\"entries_b64\"]` which is a list of base64-encoded canonical entry bytes\n4. The predicate has `from_seq`, `to_seq`, `prev_sha256`, `head_sha256`\n5. Return `None` if entries match exactly, otherwise return a problem string containing:\n   - \"range\" if count is wrong\n   - \"chain\" if an entry's `prev` doesn't link\n   - \"head\" if the last hash doesn't match `head_sha256`\n6. Wire it into wherever orphans are checked (in `cmd_monitor`)\n7. All existing tests must pass\n\nLet me look at the `cmd_monitor` function more carefully to see where orphans are checked and where I need to add the check.\n\nFrom the code, in `cmd_monitor`:\n- Line 498: `explained = {e[\"body\"][\"log_index\"]: e for e, _ in chain if e[\"kind\"] == \"orphan\"}`\n- Line 525-536: When an orphan is found, it checks the statement against Rekor's payload hash, and checks if the attested head was published and later removed\n- But there's no check for `entries_b64` in the orphan body\n\nWait, looking at the `check_body` function for orphans (lines 151-158), the allowed fields are `{\"by\", \"log_index\", \"reason\", \"statement_b64\"}`. There's no `entries_b64` field currently allowed!\n\nBut the task says `orphan[\"body\"][\"entries_b64\"]` is a list of base64-encoded canonical entry bytes. So I need to:\n1. Add `entries_b64` to the allowed fields for orphan bodies\n2. Implement the `_orphan_entries_problem` function\n3. Call it in `cmd_monitor` when checking orphans\n\nLet me first check if there are any tests for orphans with `entries_b64`. Looking at the test file, the test `test_orphan_entries_explain_attestations` creates an orphan with just `statement_b64`, no `entries_b64`.\n\nNow let me implement the solution:\n\n1. Add `entries_b64` to allowed fields for orphans\n2. Implement `_orphan_entries_problem` function\n3. Wire it into `cmd_monitor`\n\nLet me start by implementing the function.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d99b5c5f001wDmj73XE3Ki5U6","sessionID":"ses_e2664f1aeffe9y62wg3QJH9bd4","messageID":"msg_1d99b1cf80011WPSKA7ihL4aYg"}}
