{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794652234700,"sessionID":"ses_e2664f1aeffe9y62wg3QJH9bd4","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call-f6335c52-1bd3-4298-acdb-0d7d75af887e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport base64, hashlib, json\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a simple chain of 3 entries\nchain = []\nfor i in range(1, 4):\n    e = {'seq': i, 'prev': chain[-1][1] if chain else None, 'kind': 'plan',\n         'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': {'by': 'test', 'claim': f'c{i}', 'test': 't', 'decision_rule': 'd'}}\n    raw = R.canonical(e)\n    h = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n    chain.append((e, h, raw))\n\n# Test predicate for entries 2-3\npred = {'from_seq': 2, 'to_seq': 3, 'prev_sha256': chain[0][1], 'head_sha256': chain[2][1]}\n\n# Create orphan with correct entries\norphan = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(chain[1][2]).decode(), base64.b64encode(chain[2][2]).decode()]}}\nprint('Correct entries:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan, pred))\n\n# Wrong count\norphan2 = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(chain[1][2]).decode()]}}\nprint('Wrong count:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan2, pred))\n\n# Broken chain\nbad_raw = R.canonical({'seq': 2, 'prev': 'wrong', 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': {'by': 'test', 'claim': 'c2', 'test': 't', 'decision_rule': 'd'}})\norphan3 = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(bad_raw).decode(), base64.b64encode(chain[2][2]).decode()]}}\nprint('Broken chain:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan3, pred))\n\n# Wrong head\norphan4 = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(chain[1][2]).decode(), base64.b64encode(chain[2][2]).decode()]}}\npred4 = {'from_seq': 2, 'to_seq': 3, 'prev_sha256': chain[0][1], 'head_sha256': 'wrong'}\nprint('Wrong head:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan4, pred4))\n\""},"output":"Correct entries: None\nWrong count: range count 1 != expected 2\nBroken chain: chain broken at index 0: prev 'wrong' != '80b6f3b029e23423bf76dc2093fb24ad9e5b285bd10e555e86c9d7bf1690e0c1'\nWrong head: head 493e267817caf0aa00ea5316a220ddc0faf7a9a4bf55bb5586a00bc9dc560ef3 != wrong\n","metadata":{"output":"Correct entries: None\nWrong count: range count 1 != expected 2\nBroken chain: chain broken at index 0: prev 'wrong' != '80b6f3b029e23423bf76dc2093fb24ad9e5b285bd10e555e86c9d7bf1690e0c1'\nWrong head: head 493e267817caf0aa00ea5316a220ddc0faf7a9a4bf55bb5586a00bc9dc560ef3 != wrong\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"cd /workspace/record && python3 -c \"\nimport base64, hashlib, json\nimport record as R\n\n# Create a simple chain of 3 entries\nchain = []\nfor i in range(1, 4):\n    e = {'seq': i, 'prev': chain[-1][1] if chain else None, 'kind': 'plan',\n         'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': {'by': 'test', 'claim': f'c{i}', 'test': 't', 'decision_rule': 'd'}}\n    raw = R.canonical(e)\n    h = hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest()\n    chain.append((e, h, raw))\n\n# Test predicate for entries 2-3\npred = {'from_seq': 2, 'to_seq': 3, 'prev_sha256': chain[0][1], 'head_sha256': chain[2][1]}\n\n# Create orphan with correct entries\norphan = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(chain[1][2]).decode(), base64.b64encode(chain[2][2]).decode()]}}\nprint('Correct entries:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan, pred))\n\n# Wrong count\norphan2 = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(chain[1][2]).decode()]}}\nprint('Wrong count:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan2, pred))\n\n# Broken chain\nbad_raw = R.canonical({'seq': 2, 'prev': 'wrong', 'kind': 'plan', 'written_at': '2024-01-01T00:00:00Z', 'body': {'by': 'test', 'claim': 'c2', 'test': 't', 'decision_rule': 'd'}})\norphan3 = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(bad_raw).decode(), base64.b64encode(chain[2][2]).decode()]}}\nprint('Broken chain:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan3, pred))\n\n# Wrong head\norphan4 = {'body': {'entries_b64': [base64.b64encode(chain[1][2]).decode(), base64.b64encode(chain[2][2]).decode()]}}\npred4 = {'from_seq': 2, 'to_seq': 3, 'prev_sha256': chain[0][1], 'head_sha256': 'wrong'}\nprint('Wrong head:', R._orphan_entries_problem(orphan4, pred4))\n\"","time":{"start":1794652234642,"end":1794652234690}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All tests pass. Let me also verify that the function works correctly by writing a quick test to make sure the logic is correct. But first, let me check if there's any edge case I might have missed.\n\nLet me review the function again:\n- It checks the count of entries matches `to_seq - from_seq + 1`\n- It checks each entry's `prev` field chains correctly from `prev_sha256`\n- It checks the final hash matches `head_sha256`\n- Returns appropriate error strings containing \"range\", \"chain\", or \"head\"\n\nThe tests pass, so the implementation seems correct. Let me also run a quick manual test to verify the function behavior.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1d99be38d001HEm6jEVcEZKtnn","sessionID":"ses_e2664f1aeffe9y62wg3QJH9bd4","messageID":"msg_1d99bb298001X47K8P7biUqhyb"}}
